	2150 [label="Transcript: For so long the Orokin Empire had no enemies. Its military existed merely to pursue petty grudges, house against house, Executor against Executor.",shape=box,color=blue];
		2150 -> 2153;
	2153 [label="When the Sentients attacked, we knew a unity long denied to us. The Dax drew their swords against something other than an insolent peasant or a larcenous trader.",shape=box,color=blue];
		2153 -> 2154;
	2154 [label="The Emperors, the deathless titular rulers of the Empire whose power was vested in the Executors, lurched awake on their dusty golden thrones.",shape=box,color=blue];
		2154 -> 5683;
	5683 [label="War, magnificent war! At last, the Empire meant something. Defined by an extinction more imminent than the Sun’s eventual death, we drank deep of the nectar of life.",shape=box,color=blue];
